            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-17",
                    "linecount": 9,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 20.0, 480.0, 704.0, 127.0 ],
                    "text": "[mUnit.teardown] bangs its outlet once the handler has frozen the results of the patch it is in: after the result files are written (or, when a sequential harness runs the patches one at a time, before this patch is closed). The handler waits for every teardown to say it is done before it goes on, up to `teardownMs` (default 2000 ms).\n\nBy default the object reports done as soon as its outlet has fired. With `@hold 1` it waits for a message (e.g. `done`) on its inlet, for cleanup that takes time.\n\nConsole errors while a teardown runs are kept in the log but never fail the suite. The results are already final: a teardown can't change a verdict, but in sequential mode an assert fed by a teardown still registers a result, so don't do that."
                }
            }
        ],
